window.EN={"1":"Having defeated Arcardo, former Governor-General of Etruria's Western Isles,","2":"Roy and the others march east, ever east, through the snow-and-ice-bound land of Ilia.","3":"Then, as Roy and his Etrurian army advanced into Ilia's uniquely deep forest belt,","4":"using ancient great magic thought to have already been lost,","5":"the Bern army stationed in Ilia, led by priest-general Martel of the Bern Northern Army, meaning to meet Roy and the others in battle,","6":"lay waiting for them...","7":"Priest Martel! I've brought Lady Niime as ordered.","8":"Good. Let her through.","9":"What business do you have with little old me?","10":"Are you the \"Hermit of the Mountain,\" Niime?","11":"Some call me that, yes. Niime is most certainly who I am.","12":"I've heard that you can use the ancient tomes of magic from the age of the \"Scouring,\" kept here in this castle.","13":"Is that true?","14":"I wouldn't say I can't use them.","15":"After all, I'm a dark mage. I've spent several decades studying ancient magic.","16":"I hear that tome can be used to control the weather...","17":"Well, it's not that I couldn't make it happen, at least.","18":"Then I command you: use that tome to bring down a massive rain.","19":"Flood the river's waters,","20":"and halt the advance of the Etrurian army now pushing in close.","21":"Even if you say that, I don't actually know what'll happen.","22":"What's more, that type of tome can only be used once.","23":"Grrr! Just do as you're told!","24":"You came to us yourself, saying you wanted to join our army, did you not! I heard as much!","25":"Then show us now—make yourself useful to us!","26":".........","27":"Princess Guinevere...","28":"From here on, our army will be drawing closer to Bern.","29":"...Yes.","30":"Along with that, the chances of fighting Bern's soldiers are increasing too.","31":"Before long, it will surely come to a full-scale war against the kingdom of Bern's army.","32":".........","33":"Before that happens, there's something I'd like to ask you, Princess.","34":"What might it be?","35":"It's something I heard from someone the other day.","36":"That King Zephiel laid hands on Bern's former king—his own true father—and took the throne that way...","37":"!!","38":"I couldn't bring myself to believe that story was true.","39":"Because, isn't that so!","40":"Princess Guinevere, you went so far as to resolve to abandon your own country,","41":"in order to try to stop him.","42":"If King Zephiel really were the kind of cruel man the story makes him out to be,","43":"there's no way the princess would think to go that far, is there?","44":".........","45":"The reason I","46":"was entrusted by you with the \"Fire Emblem\"","47":"wasn't simply to fight against Bern,","48":"but because I thought to search, to the very end, for the \"path to peace\" the princess wished for.","49":"Lord Roy...","50":"So please, won't you let me hear the truth from your own lips, Princess?","51":"I'm sorry... please give me... just a little time.","52":"! Princess Guinevere!!","53":"...Is something the matter?","54":"Princess Guinevere went running off, which is unusual for her...","55":"...No, it's nothing. More to the point, what did you need, Marinas?","56":"I've been gathering all sorts of information, and it seems things are about to get troublesome.","57":"Among the enemy there seems to be a dark mage named Niime, said to be one of the finest in all Ilia.","58":"A dark mage... you mean a Druid.","59":"They say she's well-versed in ancient magic, and the depth of her knowledge is beyond measure, or so it's said...","60":"But there's no way we can retreat here.","61":"Of course not. Still, there's nothing better than being careful...","62":"I know. Let's stay on our guard!","63":"This is a statue of the goddess of good fortune, or so I'd always heard...","64":"I polish it every day and pray to it, but nothing good ever happens.","65":"That merchant—he tricked me, he did.","66":"Well, take it anyway. Just looking at it makes my blood boil.","67":"Hey, hey—earlier, when I was out on a walk,","68":"this came falling down out of the sky.","69":"...A god, up in the heavens? Silly, there's no way that's it.","70":"It was surely some wyvern knight or pegasus knight who dropped it.","71":"Here, you can have it. I like dolls better anyway.","72":"You folks are from the Etrurian army, aren't you.","73":"Before this, some men from Bern's army were prowling around nearby,","74":"and I wonder, when in the world will the world become peaceful?","75":"I'll give you this, so please, hurry and bring the war to an end.","76":"You lot, could it be that you're the Etrurian army that old woman was talking about?","77":"That old woman, apparently, had really meant to join your army,","78":"but instead she wandered off to the Bern lot's side... I wonder what she's thinking.","79":"You all look quite strong.","80":"But I hear that in some country, there's an incredibly strong person called the \"Sword Saint.\"","81":"That priest Martel staying at the castle is a sly one.","82":"He was saying he had some kind of trick up his sleeve.","83":"Well, a man like that is bound to destroy himself in the end, surely.","84":"Once deep winter comes, the rivers around here freeze solid, rock hard.","85":"You could easily reach the eastern village then, but","86":"it's not that season yet, so no luck.","87":"※If Martel survives","88":"Hey! Is the magic ready yet, is it ready!","89":"...I really don't know what's going to happen, you know.","90":"I don't care, hurry it up!","91":"Good grief, there's no helping it, I suppose...","92":"Wh-what in the world... is this...","93":"Is it the enemy's magic? Everyone, stay alert!","94":"Wh-what in the world... is this! The river— the river is frozen solid!","95":"Oh my, oh my... to think it would come to this.","96":"You wretch! You did that on purpose!!","97":"What are you talking about? I did say I don't know what'll happen, didn't I...","98":"Argh, silence! Someone, throw this woman in the dungeon!","99":"Yes, sir!","100":"Good grief...","101":"What on earth just happened...","102":"Lord Roy, a report has just come in. It seems the river has frozen over!","103":"What!","104":"What's more, it seems the ice has become thick enough that even knights can cross without it breaking.","105":"Good. This will make it easier for us to advance.","106":"Everyone! Let's aim straight for the enemy's castle, all at once!","107":"To think they'd push this deep into our territory, in all this snow...","108":"Damn it! That useless old hag!","109":"No, this can't be...","110":"I, who was praised as a brilliant tactician...","111":"Good grief, at last... to be freed from the Bern lot.","112":"And you are?","113":"Me, you ask?","114":"I'm just someone called Niime.","115":"I do things like study ancient dark magic, deep in the mountains.","116":"You said \"freed,\" but didn't you join Bern's army of your own will?","117":"Ho ho ho, that was just a means to an end, a means to an end. There was something I wanted to know, in Bern's army.","118":"Something you wanted to know?","119":"The \"dragons,\" that's what.","120":"!!","121":"Oh my, your color changed. It seems you have some idea of what I mean.","122":"...Not the wyverns that wyvern knights ride, but... something in Bern's army itself...","123":"That's right, that's exactly it.","124":"Those are the \"dragonkin\" that should have perished in that \"Scouring.\"","125":"How is it that you know such a thing...","126":"This commotion Bern has stirred up this time—","127":"at first I merely watched it, thinking it was just some ordinary war,","128":"but it did seem like something ominous was mixed in among the soldiers.","129":"It piqued my curiosity, so I looked into it.","130":"Did you find out anything?","131":"No, not really—I didn't get very far. There are too many mysteries when it comes to the \"dragons.\"","132":"I even stole a look at the ancient documents kept by Bern's army,","133":"but I didn't turn up much of anything worthwhile. Except... just one thing.","134":"...Just one thing?","135":"Those fellows may well have revived the \"Dragon-Devil,\" perhaps...","136":"The \"Dragon-Devil\"... you mean the one the hero Hartmut is said to have slain, the chief of the dragons?","137":"That's right.","138":"To begin with, \"dragons\" are, in both vitality and intelligence,","139":"overwhelmingly superior creatures compared to us \"humans.\"","140":"But the power to bear young...","141":"the power to increase their numbers seems to have been decisively inferior to that of \"humans.\"","142":"That, it's thought, is the decisive reason behind the outcome of the \"Scouring.\"","143":"So that's how it was... I'm learning this for the first time.","144":"Well, it's still only a hypothesis.","145":"But— but here's the thing.","146":"In a certain old document, it's said only the \"Dragon-Devil\" alone had the power to give birth to many \"dragons\"...","147":"That's what was written.","148":"In other words, Bern revived the \"Dragon-Devil,\" and is making use of the \"dragons\" it had made?","149":"...What an impatient child you are. But well, that's about the gist of it.","150":"Now, I have something to discuss with you.","151":"What is it?","152":"I'd like to solve more of the mysteries surrounding the \"dragons.\"","153":"Won't you let me travel along with you all? You won't lose out by it either.","154":"...Understood.","155":"When it comes to the \"dragons,\" there's plenty we'd like to know too.","156":"There may well be danger involved, but if you're still fine with that, let's go together."};
